course: dictionary
lesson: 13306
title: Words for big ideas
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Greatness is a noun. A noun is a naming word for a person, place, thing or idea. You can have greatness or show greatness, but it is an idea, so you cannot count it like apples. «Everyone watched the greatness of the young runner on the last lap.» Here greatness means she was very skilled.
explain: Greatness can mean three things: being important or famous, being very good and kind in character, or being very big in size. The words around it give the clue. Ask: is the sentence about fame, goodness or size? «Her greatness as a leader was shown when she helped everyone in the town.» The help tells you it is about goodness and wisdom.
explain: Look for phrases. «Achieve greatness» means to become very successful. «True greatness» means real goodness that shows in how you treat other people.
fact: Greatness is a noun, a naming word for an idea.
fact: Greatness is uncountable: you do not say two greatnesses, you say signs of greatness.
fact: «Greatness» can mean being very important, powerful, skilled or famous, being very good, wise or noble in character, or having great size.
fact: In history and stories, greatness often describes famous leaders, artists and athletes, as in «the greatness of Shakespeare».
fact: In church life, people speak of the greatness of God.
exercise: «Her greatness as a painter made her famous across the country.» What does greatness mean here? | Being very small | Being very late | Being very cold | *Being very skilled and famous
exercise: «He showed true greatness when he shared his lunch with the new boy.» What kind of greatness is this? | Being very loud | Being very rich in money | Being very tall | *Being very good and kind in character
exercise: «The greatness of the mountain made the village look tiny.» What does greatness mean in this sentence? | *Great size | Being kind to animals | Being famous for winning | Being wise in school
test: Ella says, «Achieve greatness» means to become very successful over time. What does achieve greatness mean? | To lose a race | To buy something big | *To become very successful and important | To sleep well every night
test: Which meaning fits «the greatness of the ocean made the little boat look tiny»? | Being very famous | Being very wise | *Great size | Being very kind
exam: Jayden writes, «Signs of greatness appeared early in the young singer.» What does greatness mean here? | *Being very skilled and admired | Being very wet | Being very hungry | Being very old
